<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lourdes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lourdes is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hautes-pyrenees">Hautes-Pyrénées</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>. Its castle on a rock above the Gave de Pau was the chief stronghold of the counts of Bigorre and was held by the English for decades after 1360. Since the reported apparitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a> to Bernadette Soubirous in 1858 it has been one of the largest Catholic pilgrimage sites in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lourdes.jpg" alt="Lourdes" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: X wo nd · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lourdes_city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
